{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":121083,"name":"Guido van Rossum","username":"guido","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/guido/{size}/21_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-13T13:30:46.234Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eAt the core dev sprint in Brno we decided to create a C API Working Group. The initial WG members have written a draft process PEP: \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0731/\"\u003ePEP 731\u003c/a\u003e. The GitHub file is \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/python/peps/blob/main/peps/pep-0731.rst\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is the official discussion thread for this PEP! Please review the draft PEP and discuss it here. We’ll follow the usual (sometimes chaotic) PEP discussion process and once we feel there’s rough consensus we’ll seek approval of the Steering Council.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere are also two new GitHub repos for conversations (although what will happen to these depends on how this PEP fares):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/capi-workgroup/api-evolution\"\u003eAPI Evolution\u003c/a\u003e (for gradually evolving the existing C API – we expect another PEP to come out of this)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/capi-workgroup/api-revolution\"\u003eAPI Revolution\u003c/a\u003e (for disruptive proposals, each of which will require a PEP by itself to make any chance)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd of course there’s the earlier \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/capi-workgroup/problems\"\u003eproblems repo\u003c/a\u003e, which will be turned into an informational PEP (regardless of whether PEP 731 is accepted).\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":13,"updated_at":"2023-10-13T13:41:01.910Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":426,"reads":185,"readers_count":184,"score":2362.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":36117,"topic_slug":"pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter","display_username":"Guido van Rossum","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0731/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 731 – C API Working Group Charter | peps.python.org","clicks":109},{"url":"https://github.com/capi-workgroup/api-revolution","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - capi-workgroup/api-revolution: Proposals for radical or controversial API changes","clicks":22},{"url":"https://github.com/capi-workgroup/api-evolution","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - capi-workgroup/api-evolution: Issues related to evolution of the C API","clicks":20},{"url":"https://github.com/python/peps/blob/main/peps/pep-0731.rst","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":20},{"url":"https://github.com/capi-workgroup/problems","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - capi-workgroup/problems: Discussions about problems with the current C Api","clicks":15}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":13}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":10,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter/36117/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":13}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":13,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":121119,"name":"Terry Jan Reedy","username":"tjreedy","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/tjreedy/{size}/137_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-13T18:03:06.968Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eLooks good to me, including the initial membership.  Love the Epigraph.  Aaargh indeed!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":13,"updated_at":"2023-10-13T18:03:06.968Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":175,"readers_count":174,"score":85.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":36117,"topic_slug":"pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter","display_username":"Terry Jan Reedy","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":110,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter/36117/2","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":3,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":121446,"name":"Itamar Oren","username":"itamaro","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/itamaro/{size}/20137_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-15T17:53:58.629Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThis looks great - a promising venue for a more organized and intentional evolution of the C API!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA few thoughts and questions on the PEP:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe working group has at least three members, comprised of prominent Python core developers. The members should consider the needs of the various stakeholders carefully.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConsidering “the various stakeholders” include “all users of Python, especially maintainers of code that uses the C API […]” - why limit membership in the working group to core developers?\u003cbr\u003e\nI do think it’s crucial to include “prominent core devs” (btw what is “prominent” exactly?) in order to represent the interest of the maintainers of the C API. I can’t imagine such a working group without \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/vstinner\"\u003e@vstinner\u003c/a\u003e \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/apple/sweat_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":sweat_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":sweat_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e for example. Why not include members representing “prominent stakeholders”, like HPy, PyPy, Cython, pybind11, … - even if they are not core developers?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlso, what happens if for whatever reason the working group membership drops below 3 members? Is it disbanded? Is it “frozen” until membership grows back?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe working group’s mandate is to ensure that the Python C API is suitable for all users of and contributors to the API\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIs the scope here well-defined (or intentionally fuzzy)?\u003cbr\u003e\nFor example, should the working group govern the “technically public (as in, can be used by invoking an incantation of includes and defines) but not officially public” API? What about the unstable API?\u003cbr\u003e\nConcretely, will core devs need to seek the approval of the working group when introducing, removing, or changing “private” (\u003ccode\u003e_Py...\u003c/code\u003e) or unstable APIs?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":13,"updated_at":"2023-10-15T17:53:58.629Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":151,"readers_count":150,"score":85.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":36117,"topic_slug":"pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter","display_username":"Itamar Oren","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":5601,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter/36117/3","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":3,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":121461,"name":"Terry Jan Reedy","username":"tjreedy","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/tjreedy/{size}/137_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-15T19:35:44.386Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eTo me, ‘prominent’ means respected, trusted to consider all stakeholders and balance change versus stability.  I not sure what adjective would be better.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI expect stakeholder representatives to be biased and argue in favor of the needs of their particular projects.  That is their self-chosen job, so to speak.  I expect that they will continue to contribute their viewpoints as further PEPs are proposed.  I was not at the sprint, but agree that the proposed group is more likely to produce viable proposals than a mixed group of several stakeholders.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":13,"updated_at":"2023-10-15T19:35:44.386Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":142,"readers_count":141,"score":58.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":36117,"topic_slug":"pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter","display_username":"Terry Jan Reedy","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":110,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter/36117/4","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":121617,"name":"Victor Stinner","username":"vstinner","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/vstinner/{size}/15130_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-16T19:45:00.834Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"itamaro\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"36117\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/itamaro/48/20137_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Itamar Oren:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConcretely, will core devs need to seek the approval of the working group when introducing, removing, or changing “private” (\u003ccode\u003e_Py...\u003c/code\u003e) or unstable APIs?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI don’t think that the plan is to hold any PR touching Include/ until all members of the C API Working Group approve it. It’s more about defining guidelines and seeking consensus on C API changes, and taking decisions on technical questions on the C API, than reviewing every single C API change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor example, I’m interested by no longer allowing to add new \u003cstrong\u003eprivate\u003c/strong\u003e API (\u003cem\u003ePy prefix, but not doc nor tests) in the C API: an API should be either public (\u003ccode\u003ePy\u003c/code\u003e prefix, exported, tested, documented) or internal (\u003ccode\u003e_Py\u003c/code\u003e prefix, usually not exported, need Py_BUILD_CORE, special include with pycore\u003c/em\u003e prefix). PyUnstable is part of the public API (\u003ccode\u003ePy\u003c/code\u003e prefix, exported, tested, documented), only the backward compatibility policy changes (\u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0689/\"\u003ePEP 689\u003c/a\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":13,"updated_at":"2023-10-16T19:45:58.645Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":3,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":7,"reads":134,"readers_count":133,"score":81.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":36117,"topic_slug":"pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter","display_username":"Victor Stinner","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0689/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 689 – Unstable C API tier | peps.python.org","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":13,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter/36117/5","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":121731,"name":"Petr Viktorin","username":"encukou","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/encukou/{size}/2461_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-17T11:43:47.905Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"itamaro\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"36117\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/itamaro/48/20137_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Itamar Oren:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ewhat happens if for whatever reason the working group membership drops below 3 members? Is it disbanded? Is it “frozen” until membership grows back?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Steering Council can step in and decide. Like in any unforeseen/ambiguous/harmful situation.\u003cbr\u003e\nThis PEP doesn’t really need to be a bulletproof charter.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"itamaro\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"36117\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/itamaro/48/20137_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Itamar Oren:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConcretely, will core devs need to seek the approval of the working group when introducing, removing, or changing “private” (\u003ccode\u003e_Py...\u003c/code\u003e) or unstable APIs?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIMO: No, but it’d be good to follow the public-API guidelines where they make sense.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"itamaro\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"36117\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/itamaro/48/20137_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Itamar Oren:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy not include members representing “prominent stakeholders”, like HPy, PyPy, Cython, pybind11, … - even if they are not core developers?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIMO, if they are trusted enough, they should be promoted to core developers.\u003cbr\u003e\nThe working group is small, so its members must take other viewpoints than their own into account. We can’t add every stakeholder directly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers quote-modified\" data-username=\"vstinner\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"36117\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/vstinner/48/15130_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Victor Stinner:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eprivate\u003c/strong\u003e API (\u003cem\u003ePy prefix, but not doc nor tests)\u003c/em\u003e […] \u003cem\u003einternal (\u003ccode\u003e_Py\u003c/code\u003e prefix, usually not exported, need Py_BUILD_CORE, special include with pycore\u003c/em\u003e prefix)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt might be useful to define the terms “private”/“internal” in a PEP, devguide or docs. Their meaning seems to subtly change every time I look at them…\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cem\u003eEdit: I filed this as \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/capi-workgroup/api-evolution/issues/33\"\u003e#33 in the WG repo\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":13,"updated_at":"2023-10-23T08:35:10.540Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":3,"quote_count":2,"incoming_link_count":4,"reads":130,"readers_count":129,"score":96.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":36117,"topic_slug":"pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter","display_username":"Petr Viktorin","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/capi-workgroup/api-evolution/issues/33","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Define “private” and “internal” · Issue #33 · capi-workgroup/api-evolution · GitHub","clicks":4}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":26,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter/36117/6","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":3,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":122233,"name":"Simon Cross","username":"hodgestar","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/hodgestar/{size}/8749_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-19T21:18:27.944Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI second the idea of having someone prominent from the C extension community join the WG, but happy for the WG itself to add such members.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI don’t know whether the requirement to be a core developer hinders adding such members or not. I would assume that, e.g., a core numpy developer, already fulfills many of the requirements and simply being willing to put time into the C API WG might make them qualify?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":13,"updated_at":"2023-10-19T21:18:27.944Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":122,"readers_count":121,"score":59.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":36117,"topic_slug":"pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter","display_username":"Simon Cross","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":8528,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter/36117/7","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":122295,"name":"Steve Dower","username":"steve.dower","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/steve.dower/{size}/56_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-20T12:17:12.853Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eSince the WG would be proposing changes that are only directly binding on the core development team, I’m okay with the core developer requirement.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the WG doesn’t appear to be soliciting contributions from prominent users of the API and factoring them in, that’s a reason to go to the steering council with a complaint.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeing directly on the WG isn’t a prerequisite to contribute. It’s just a burden of having to take responsibility for the decisions and how they impact other competing interests.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":13,"updated_at":"2023-10-20T12:17:12.853Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":8,"reads":125,"readers_count":124,"score":110.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":36117,"topic_slug":"pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter","display_username":"Steve Dower","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":54,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter/36117/8","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":3,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":122425,"name":"Guido van Rossum","username":"guido","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/guido/{size}/21_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-21T01:14:45.135Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"encukou\" data-post=\"6\" data-topic=\"36117\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/encukou/48/2461_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Petr Viktorin:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt might be useful to define the terms “private”/“internal” in a PEP, devguide or docs. Their meaning seems to subtly change every time I look at them…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis feels off-topic for the WG charter, but I wholeheartedly agree that these terms can be used confusingly. The WG, once established, should discuss this topic and come up with agreed-upon, useful and future-proof definitions of the terms. But not right now.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":13,"updated_at":"2023-10-21T01:14:45.135Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":4,"reads":122,"readers_count":121,"score":59.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":36117,"topic_slug":"pep-731-c-api-working-group-charter","display_username":"Guido van Rossum","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core 